window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Every journey must end one way or another.</p> <p>And in Declan's experience, that usually means death.</p> <p>Death of his enemies. Death of his friends.</p> <p>Their one hope of surviving is in the hands of a man he wants to see suffer—even if it means letting the darkness within take over.</p> <p>But even if he retrieves the dagger, he could still lose everything.</p> <p>He could still lose her.</p> <p>He may not be good enough—he may not deserve her—but he's not about to let her go.</p> <p>Not without a fight.</p> <p>This is the final book in the Aisling Sea series. Darker, grittier, and spicier, this book contains anxiety representation, torture, violence, family drama, and intimate scenes.</p>"; 
